+  // Absolute schedule: returns once now_ns() >= due, false as soon as the source stops (stop wakes the
+  // condition variable; the precise tail below is <= 3 ms). `due` is on now_ns()'s clock (steady_clock, counts
+  // sleep), mach_wait_until on host time (stops in sleep): the tail is waited as a host deadline made from the
+  // time LEFT and the host clock's own now, never by reading `due` as a host time (F4: after the Mac had slept
+  // 168 s, each frame waited 168 s and the stop's join hung).
+  bool wait_until(int64_t due) {
+    std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lk(mu_);
